{"caveats":"The police value is specifically the Year 1 entry step for officers hired after 1999, while the Code Enforcement Officer line provides a single listed rate with no tenure, step, or experience label. The source establishes common municipality, cycle, page, hourly pay basis, and schedule-listed wage status, but it does not establish comparable tenure, experience, duties, qualifications, hours, full-time status, or schedule position. The upstream normalized Code Enforcement Officer record was incorrectly tagged as police; this validation corrects the candidate interpretation from the verbatim source line but does not overwrite the raw upstream record. The negative $0.91/hour documentary difference pertains only to these two specifically listed schedule values and must not be generalized to police and non-safety employees in Canastota. This is bounded local documentary evidence, not a final wage-gap estimate, and is not nationally representative. Substantive/manual validation of occupational and schedule-position comparability is required before analytic use beyond a qualified supporting example.","claim_boundary":"conditional_with_caveats","confidence":"moderate","local_comparison_record_id":"B4X2500GAP-498d2fdd8da985bf2455ab27","municipality":"Canastota","no_causal_claim":true,"non_safety_side_label":"non_safety","period":"2023-2024","qa_status":"conditional_example_ready","safety_side_label":"safety","source_layer":"BROAD-STATE-4X2500-BOUNDED-WAGE-DIFFERENTIAL-VALIDATION-2026-07-30","source_lineage":"{\"candidate_id\": \"B4X2500LIVE-20260729-006395\", \"extracted_text_sha256\": \"fd41d71ce599f0645d2985c6eab82248e01481503a1aa34c6fd8b86ec45ac2c6\", \"extraction_id\": \"B4X2500TXT-20260730-00970d81537bd8db1772\", \"lineage_integrity\": \"passed; local retained-source and extracted-text hashes match the tracked manifests\", \"readiness_id\": \"B4X2500RDY-20260730-a8d3be473679172d086a\", \"retained_source_page_count\": 17, \"retained_source_sha256\": \"719a57b